[{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":18,"col":24},"end":{"line":18,"col":33}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`elementof` describes a result, and this is a parameter.\n\n`fresh`, `exclusive` and `unknown` say what a call returns, so they stand in\nfront of the type after the last `→`. A parameter takes `unused`, `borrowed`,\n`aliased`, `returned`, `escaped` or `consumed`."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":21,"col":49},"end":{"line":21,"col":58}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"The ownership word `elementof` cannot hold together with another word written\nhere.\n\nA result is one of `fresh`, `escaped`, `unknown`, `taken`, `lent`,\n`lentoptional`, `cellnew`, `cellempty`, `builderdone`, `concatenated`,\n`elementof`, `copyof` and `prepended`. A parameter does one thing to a cell:\n`cellread`, `cellwrite` or `cellcomplete`.\n`cellupdate` and `cellmodify` say already that the callback is called once and\nis handed the contents owned, so they stand without `once`, `many`, `taken`,\n`owned` and each other."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":24,"col":50},"end":{"line":24,"col":56}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"The ownership word `copyof` cannot hold together with another word written here.\n\nA result is one of `fresh`, `escaped`, `unknown`, `taken`, `lent`,\n`lentoptional`, `cellnew`, `cellempty`, `builderdone`, `concatenated`,\n`elementof`, `copyof` and `prepended`. A parameter does one thing to a cell:\n`cellread`, `cellwrite` or `cellcomplete`.\n`cellupdate` and `cellmodify` say already that the callback is called once and\nis handed the contents owned, so they stand without `once`, `many`, `taken`,\n`owned` and each other."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":27,"col":46},"end":{"line":27,"col":55}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`elementof` needs words on the parameters, and one is missing or contradicts it.\n\n`elementof` says that the result is an element of the first parameter, read\nin place, so the first parameter is read and is not `unused`, `escaped` or\n`consumed`: `at : borrowed List a, borrowed Int → elementof a`. `copyof` says\nthat the result is a fresh copy of the first parameter's storage, so the first\nparameter is `borrowed`: `copy : borrowed List a → copyof List a`. `prepended`\nsays that the result is the first parameter put in front of the second, so\nthere are exactly two parameters: `cons : stored a, returned List a →\nprepended List a`."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":30,"col":43},"end":{"line":30,"col":49}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`copyof` needs words on the parameters, and one is missing or contradicts it.\n\n`elementof` says that the result is an element of the first parameter, read\nin place, so the first parameter is read and is not `unused`, `escaped` or\n`consumed`: `at : borrowed List a, borrowed Int → elementof a`. `copyof` says\nthat the result is a fresh copy of the first parameter's storage, so the first\nparameter is `borrowed`: `copy : borrowed List a → copyof List a`. `prepended`\nsays that the result is the first parameter put in front of the second, so\nthere are exactly two parameters: `cons : stored a, returned List a →\nprepended List a`."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":33,"col":57},"end":{"line":33,"col":66}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`prepended` needs words on the parameters, and one is missing or contradicts it.\n\n`elementof` says that the result is an element of the first parameter, read\nin place, so the first parameter is read and is not `unused`, `escaped` or\n`consumed`: `at : borrowed List a, borrowed Int → elementof a`. `copyof` says\nthat the result is a fresh copy of the first parameter's storage, so the first\nparameter is `borrowed`: `copy : borrowed List a → copyof List a`. `prepended`\nsays that the result is the first parameter put in front of the second, so\nthere are exactly two parameters: `cons : stored a, returned List a →\nprepended List a`."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":36,"col":54},"end":{"line":36,"col":63}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`prepended` needs words on the parameters, and one is missing or contradicts it.\n\n`elementof` says that the result is an element of the first parameter, read\nin place, so the first parameter is read and is not `unused`, `escaped` or\n`consumed`: `at : borrowed List a, borrowed Int → elementof a`. `copyof` says\nthat the result is a fresh copy of the first parameter's storage, so the first\nparameter is `borrowed`: `copy : borrowed List a → copyof List a`. `prepended`\nsays that the result is the first parameter put in front of the second, so\nthere are exactly two parameters: `cons : stored a, returned List a →\nprepended List a`."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":39,"col":56},"end":{"line":39,"col":62}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`stored` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":42,"col":58},"end":{"line":42,"col":64}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`stored` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":45,"col":65},"end":{"line":45,"col":71}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`stored` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":48,"col":57},"end":{"line":48,"col":63}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`stored` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":51,"col":27},"end":{"line":51,"col":36}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`cellwrite` needs another word beside it, and that word is missing.\n\nThese words name the roles of several parameters together: `cellnew` needs a\n`consumed` first parameter, `cellempty` an `unused` one, `lent` and\n`lentoptional` a `cellread` one; `cellwrite` needs a second parameter that is\n`cellstored`, `cellupdate` or `cellmodify`, and `cellcomplete` one that is\n`cellstored`; `cellstored` is `consumed` and follows `cellwrite` or\n`cellcomplete`; `builderdone` needs a `written returned` first parameter and a\nsecond, its length, at most `borrowed`; `concatenated` a `written` first\nparameter and exactly one more; a `taken` result or function parameter a\ncontainer before it that is not `unused`. Write the missing word, or remove\nthis one."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":51,"col":44},"end":{"line":51,"col":54}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`cellupdate` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":54,"col":29},"end":{"line":54,"col":38}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`cellwrite` needs another word beside it, and that word is missing.\n\nThese words name the roles of several parameters together: `cellnew` needs a\n`consumed` first parameter, `cellempty` an `unused` one, `lent` and\n`lentoptional` a `cellread` one; `cellwrite` needs a second parameter that is\n`cellstored`, `cellupdate` or `cellmodify`, and `cellcomplete` one that is\n`cellstored`; `cellstored` is `consumed` and follows `cellwrite` or\n`cellcomplete`; `builderdone` needs a `written returned` first parameter and a\nsecond, its length, at most `borrowed`; `concatenated` a `written` first\nparameter and exactly one more; a `taken` result or function parameter a\ncontainer before it that is not `unused`. Write the missing word, or remove\nthis one."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":54,"col":46},"end":{"line":54,"col":56}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`cellmodify` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":60,"col":18},"end":{"line":60,"col":24}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`stored` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."},{"code":"misplaced_ownership_word","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/check/bad/core/MisplacedResultSelector.beni","start":{"line":66,"col":15},"end":{"line":66,"col":23}},"title":"MISPLACED OWNERSHIP WORD","message":"`returned` describes a callback whose answer is stored, and a word it needs is\nmissing or another word contradicts it.\n\n`stored` in front of a function parameter stores what the callback returns.\nWithout a cell word the answer goes back where the element it was handed came\nfrom: the callback is `once taken stored` and the first parameter is `written\nreturned`, as in `focus : written returned List a, borrowed Int, once taken\nstored (a → a) → List a`. With a cell word the answer goes back into the cell,\nand the cell word needs `stored`: `cellupdate stored sync (a → a)` stores the\nwhole answer, `cellmodify stored sync (a → b × a)` its second part. The\ncallback is one function written out, not a `List` of them, and it is not\nalso `many`, `returned`, `aliased`, `escaped` or `unused`. One callback puts\nits answer back, into the first parameter alone: a second such callback, or a\nsecond `written returned` parameter beside it, is refused."}]
